// RUN: cd %corpus && ! %zomc compile --check 05-statements/inherent_method_call_unsupported_neg_01.zom > %t 2>&1
// RUN: %FileCheck %s --input-file %t

// The checker accepts the shared-receiver inherent call and produces its call
// facts, and the callee method body itself now builds verified semantic HIR,
// but the HIR receiver-call carrier only lowers a mutable borrow today. The
// shared call is therefore rejected on the calling definition as a capability
// gap (ZOM4099), projected at the call site, never as an internal compiler
// error.

// CHECK-LITERAL: Error [ZOM4099]: this function body uses a construct the compiler cannot generate code for yet
// CHECK-LITERAL:   --> conformance/05-statements/inherent_method_call_unsupported_neg_01.zom:8:10
